---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "About Ancient China Travel";
const description = "Who writes Ancient China Travel, why this site exists, and how every guide is researched and verified. Meet the author behind the site.";

const personSchema = {
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Alex Chen",
  "jobTitle": "Independent Travel Writer",
  "description": "Independent travel writer and archaeology enthusiast based in Hangzhou, China. Has visited every ancient Chinese archaeological site featured on this site.",
  "url": "https://5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com/about",
  "sameAs": [],
  "knowsAbout": ["Chinese Archaeology", "Ancient Chinese History", "China Travel", "Museum Booking", "Chinese Neolithic Cultures"],
};

const orgSchema = {
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "Ancient China Travel",
  "url": "https://5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com",
  "description": "Independent travel guides for ancient Chinese archaeological sites. Firsthand, passport-tested booking instructions and honest site reviews.",
  "founder": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Alex Chen" },
  "contactPoint": {
    "@type": "ContactPoint",
    "email": "hello@5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com",
    "contactType": "customer service",
  },
};

const schemaJson = JSON.stringify([
  personSchema, orgSchema,
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": "https://5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com/about" }
    ]
  },
]);
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} schemaJson={schemaJson}>
  <slot name="head">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com/og-default.webp" />
  </slot>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-warm-900 py-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-accent/80 mb-4">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-display font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-white max-w-3xl">About Ancient China Travel</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-warm-200/80 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">Who writes this site, how every guide is researched, and why we built it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who -->
  <section class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-16 reveal">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Who Writes This Site</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-accent/20 flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center text-3xl font-bold text-accent">AC</div>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>Hi, I am Alex Chen. I have lived in China for over a decade and have spent most of that time exploring archaeological sites — the famous ones, the obscure ones, and the ones that are not in any guidebook. I built Ancient China Travel because the information foreigners need to visit these sites was scattered across Chinese-language apps, outdated forum threads, and news articles that never answered the practical question: <em>"How do I actually go there?"</em></p>
        <p>I have personally visited every archaeological site featured on this site. I have booked Sanxingdui tickets through the WeChat mini-program with a foreign passport. I have taken the bus 306 to the Terracotta Warriors at 7 AM. I have walked the entire Liangzhu archaeological park in the August heat. Every price, every opening hour, and every booking instruction on this site has been tested firsthand.</p>
        <p>I am not a professional archaeologist. I am a travel writer who takes ancient history seriously and believes that walking through a 5,300-year-old city is one of the most extraordinary things a person can do. My goal is to remove every logistical barrier between you and that experience.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How -->
  <section class="bg-warm-50 py-16 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">How Every Guide Is Made</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>Every guide on this site follows the same process:</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-sm">
          <li><strong>Visit the site in person.</strong> No remote research. No paraphrasing Wikipedia. If it is not on this site, I have not been there yet.</li>
          <li><strong>Test the booking process with a foreign passport.</strong> For museum booking guides, I go through the exact WeChat mini-program flow a foreign traveler would face — selecting "Passport" as ID, entering a passport number, navigating the Chinese-only interface.</li>
          <li><strong>Verify ticket prices, hours, and transport on every visit.</strong> Things change fast in China. Prices are re-checked quarterly and updated immediately when they change. The footer always shows the last verification date.</li>
          <li><strong>Write honestly about what works and what does not.</strong> Some sites are crowded. Some booking systems are frustrating. Some places are not worth the detour. I tell you all of it.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-16 reveal">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Why This Site Exists</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>In March 2025, Chinese archaeologists uncovered a 5,000-year-old tomb in Henan Province with 350 burial objects and nearly 200 jade artifacts. The discovery made headlines worldwide — BBC, CNN, Reuters all covered it. But every article ended the same way: a period after the last paragraph, with no answer to the question readers actually had.</p>
      <p><em>"Can I go see it?"</em></p>
      <p>The answer to that specific tomb turned out to be no — it is an active excavation. But the deeper question — "What ancient Chinese archaeological sites can I actually visit?" — had no good answer online. The information existed, but it was locked inside Chinese-language WeChat mini-programs, scattered across decade-old TripAdvisor threads, or hidden behind tour-company paywalls.</p>
      <p>This site is the answer. Eight remarkable sites, all open to visitors, with the practical detail that turns curiosity into a plane ticket. No ads. No affiliate pressure. No AI-generated filler. Just the information I wish someone had given me before my first trip.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section class="bg-warm-50 py-16 reveal" id="contact">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Get in Touch</h2>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-border p-6 space-y-4 text-sm text-warm-700">
        <p>Have a question about visiting an archaeological site? Found something outdated? Want to suggest a site I should cover next? I read every email.</p>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">hello@5000-year-old-chinese-tomb.com</a></p>
        <p>I typically respond within 48 hours. If you are writing from the road and need urgent help (stuck at a train station, booking system not working), mention it in the subject line and I will reply as quickly as I can.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-warm-900 py-16 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">Ready to start planning?</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 bg-accent text-white font-medium rounded-lg hover:bg-accent-dark active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-150">Browse All Sites</a>
        <a href="/ancient-china-10-day-itinerary" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 border border-white/40 text-white font-medium rounded-lg hover:bg-white/10 active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-150">10-Day Itinerary</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
